     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p36-constructing-rates-teaching",
     "replacement": "Water poured into a container at a constant rate raises the water height at a rate that depends on the **cross-section**, the horizontal slice of the container at the water level.\n\n- **Larger** cross-section: **slower** increase in water height.\n- **Smaller** cross-section: **faster** increase in water height.\n- **Constant** cross-section: **constant** rate of increase in water height.\n\nWhen the cross-section changes as the water rises, the rate of increase changes with it.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p36-constructing-rates-teaching",
